.Dd September 11, 2026
.Dt INTEL_PMC 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm intel_pmc
.Nd Intel Performance Management Controller driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd device intel_pmc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver exposes information and controls from the Performance
Management Controller (PMC) of Intel platforms, providing access to
debug information and controls related to S0ix (Modern Standby).
.Pp
On Sunrise Point (Skylake and Kaby Lake generations) the PMC is a PCI
function and the driver attaches to it.
Later generations do not enumerate the PMC on PCI; there the driver
identifies the platform by CPU model and maps the register space at
the architectural base address.
The residency counter address in the ACPI LPIT table is compared
against that window and a mismatch is reported.
.Pp
The cumulative time spent in low power mode while in S0 is reported,
and the administrator can force the platform to ignore IP blocks
whose Latency Tolerance Reporting (LTR) prevents the platform from
entering S0ix.
.Sh HARDWARE
The
.Nm
driver supports the PMC block found in the following Intel Platform
Controller Hubs:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
Sunrise Point-LP (6th/7th Gen Core mobile)
.It
Sunrise Point-H (6th/7th Gen Core desktop/server)
.It
Cannon Lake, Comet Lake
.It
Ice Lake, Jasper Lake
.It
Tiger Lake, Elkhart Lake, Rocket Lake
.It
Alder Lake, Raptor Lake
.It
Meteor Lake
.El
.Sh SYSCTLS
The following
.Xr sysctl 8
variables are available:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va dev.intel_pmc.%d.ltr_ignore Pq read-write
Latency Tolerance Reporting (LTR) ignore mask.
Setting a bit tells the PMC to ignore that IP block's LTR requirements,
allowing S0ix entry even if the IP would otherwise block it.
The number and meaning of the bits vary by platform; consult the
datasheet listed in
.Sx SEE ALSO .
.It Va dev.intel_pmc.%d.slp_s0_residency Pq read-only
Cumulative time in microseconds that the platform has been in S0ix.
A value that never advances indicates S0ix transitions are not
occurring.
This value wraps after a few days, as the counter is 32-bit and
updated approximately every 100us (platform-dependent).
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr acpi 4 ,
.Xr pci 4 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Pp
Intel 100 Series Chipset Family PCH Datasheet, Volume 2, Section 4.3.
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Abdelkader Boudih Aq Mt seuros@FreeBSD.org
.Sh CAVEATS
Desktop firmware frequently does not implement S0ix; the driver still
attaches there, but the residency counter never advances.
Lunar Lake and later are not yet supported.
